# Custom Lib (text.ts)

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` has a fixed, three-function API — not lodash. Agents
tend to hallucinate helpers that don't exist here.

## Rule

- Only import `slugify`, `truncate`, `normalizeSpaces` from
  `app/src/lib/text.ts` — do not assume any other helper exists.
- If new text behavior is needed (e.g. capitalization), add a new named
  export function to `app/src/lib/text.ts` with a colocated test — do not
  invent a call to a nonexistent function, and do not pull in an external
  string-utility package.
- Preserve existing signatures exactly: `truncate`'s `maxLength` includes the
  suffix length; do not change this contract when extending the file.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "from \"\./lib/text" app/src \| grep -v "slugify\|truncate\|normalizeSpaces"` —
   should find zero matches importing an unknown helper.
2. Any new function added to `lib/text.ts` has a corresponding test in
   `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`.
3. `cd app && npm test` stays green.
